<DocsLayout title="Account classification">
  <h1>Account classification</h1>
  <p>
    A backend can check the current standing of one or two known account IDs
    with <code>ClassifyAccounts</code>. Each result contains only the requested
    ID and a coarse classification: denied, active known adult, or active
    known minor. A minor includes both the child and teen age bands.
    No birth date, email, name, contacts, tokens or profile fields are returned.
  </p>
  <h2>Backend credential and project</h2>
  <p>
    Create an <code>account_classifier</code> credential with
    <code>AdminCreateProjectCredential</code>. Its <code>ak_</code> raw key is
    shown once; store it encrypted on the backend and send it only in
    <code>X-Account-Classifier-Key</code>. It grants no directory lookup,
    profile, session, write or guardian authorization rights. Other credential
    kinds and user JWTs do not authorize this operation.
  </p>
  <p>
    The credential must belong to the resolved project. HTTP resolves that
    project from its normal hostname or public project key; native gRPC
    requires <code>X-Project-Key</code>. The classifier credential itself
    cannot select a project. A revoked key or suspended project is refused on
    its next call. Without a control plane and project resolver, the RPC is
    disabled with <code>UNIMPLEMENTED</code>.
  </p>
  <h2>Request and result</h2>
  <p>
    Send <code>user_ids</code> with one or two distinct exact account IDs,
    each at most 128 bytes. Email discovery, blank IDs, control characters and
    duplicate IDs are refused. The response's <code>accounts</code> list has
    exactly one result for each input in the same order.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>ACCOUNT_CLASSIFICATION_ACTIVE_KNOWN_ADULT</code>: an active permanent person with a known adult age band.</li>
    <li><code>ACCOUNT_CLASSIFICATION_ACTIVE_KNOWN_MINOR</code>: an active permanent person with a known child or teen age band.</li>
    <li><code>ACCOUNT_CLASSIFICATION_DENIED</code>: missing or foreign-project account, unknown age, anonymous or machine account, merged account, empty or unknown kind/status, or any inactive state.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Project and user-market age thresholds are read for each check. Disabled
    age gating, future or implausible birth dates yield denied. Treat an
    omitted or unknown classification, missing result or any RPC error as
    denied. A storage outage never produces a partial affirmative response.
  </p>
  <h2>Standing is separate from authorization</h2>
  <p>
    A classification grants no permission to contact someone or act for
    them. Recheck it on admission, refresh and reconciliation. Never cache an
    affirmative result. Applications must independently verify household,
    contact, consent and device rules, and call
    <code>GetManagedChildAuthorization</code> for every minor involved.
  </p>
  <h2>Capacity and audit</h2>
  <p>
    <code>GATEWAY_RATE_LIMIT_ACCOUNT_CLASSIFICATION_PER_IP</code> sets a
    separate HTTP/native shared budget per rate-limit window, default 1200.
    Zero selects the default, negative is invalid and the limit cannot be
    disabled. <code>accounts_classified</code> audit events record the
    credential actor and request count without account profiles or birth dates.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
